hypothesis: 'Longer training at the halved learning rate. Every run so far is v059
  plus a failed variation: the stack (v062) landed below baseline, and one layer instead
  of two (v063) landed tied with baseline. Training length is the one axis never tried
  at lr 1e-3. Halving the LR halves the total distance travelled per step, so the
  3-epoch budget may simply be too short at this rate -- which would make epochs and
  lr the SAME axis rather than independent ones, and that is exactly the kind of thing
  v063 just revealed elsewhere.'
